/-! The Golay octad graph and its product with two projective polarity relations give the
lower bound from Kumar, Mohar and Pragada, Section 3 (https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.02698).
Taking fields of orders 2^a and 3^b in the two relations lets the degree approximate every
sufficiently large integer using density of the subgroup generated by log 2 and log 3. -/

open Finset SimpleGraph
open scoped BigOperators

namespace KMPBase

private abbrev Vertex := Fin 506
private abbrev Point := Fin 23

/-
The octad graph is the finite construction from Kumar, Mohar and Pragada,
"An improved bound for the strong clique index of graphs", Section 3,
https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.02698.
The masks are the weight-eight multiples of the binary polynomial
(1 + X + X^5 + X^6 + X^7 + X^9 + X^{11}).
The point permutations are the cyclic shift and a Mathieu permutation from
the ATLAS of Finite Groups, conjugated by coordinate negation, https://gaetan.chenevier.perso.math.cnrs.fr/ALG1/ATLAS.pdf.
The table records their induced maps on the octads, their inverses,
a predecessor in a traversal from octad zero, and base-row common neighbors.
All properties used below are proved by kernel evaluation of this data.
-/
